   `src/cljc/yang/python/antlr/lower.cljc:258`, `:284`, `:301`; `test/yang/python/antlr/int_literal_test.cljc:262`.

   The implementation validates syntax, removes underscores, creates a per-literal public module with `max-bits = 4 × digit count`, parses exactly, compares against 2^53−1, and formats larger values in canonical lowercase hexadecimal. Radices 2/8/10/16 and uppercase prefixes are covered. The five boundary groups compare rows and bytes and assert shared address goldens.

