   Exactly one executable prelude definition is added:
   `(py/int-lit s)` delegates to `py/int-result(integer/parse s 16)`. `integer/parse` enters `host-names`, which feeds the existing closed-name check. The other additions are host-side admission definitions.

   The diff changes five float-address goldens and leaves the hook-prelude golden unchanged. Static review cannot establish how many times they were generated; the engineer reports once.

